  "description": "Family of French medical encoder (fill-mask) models from Doctolib Lab, pretrained from scratch on curated open-web medical text. Two variants — doctobert-fr-base (RoBERTa-style, ~111M params) and doctomodernbert-fr-base (ModernBERT architecture) — trained over ~700B tokens in two phases (general pretraining then biomedical/clinical annealing) on the FineMed-fr and FineMed-rephrased-fr corpora. Designed for biomedical and clinical NLP tasks: named entity recognition, classification, and retrieval. Evaluated on the public DrBenchmark suite and proprietary clinical NER, where medical-term-density filtering plus LLM rephrasing of training data yielded state-of-the-art French medical encoder results. Explicitly not generative and not a medical device. Apache-2.0, open ungated weights on Hugging Face.",
  "url": "https://huggingface.co/doctolib-lab/doctobert-fr-base",
