  "mach:weightsLicense": "Apache-2.0",
  "mach:trainingDataSummary": "Pretrained from scratch on the FineMed-fr and FineMed-rephrased-fr corpora (curated French medical text derived from FineWeb-2, FinePDFs, and FineWiki), ~700B tokens across two phases: initial pretraining followed by biomedical/clinical annealing. Training data is openly released as the FineMed dataset (cataloged separately).",
  "mach:intendedUse": "French biomedical and clinical NLP research: named entity recognition, text classification, and retrieval over medical text. An encoder for downstream fine-tuning. Not generative, not a diagnostic or clinical-decision tool, and not a cleared medical device.",
  "mach:aiActRiskClass": "limited-risk",
