  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "A current (June 2026) and openly licensed French medical encoder family — Apache-2.0 with ungated weights, a reproducible data-curation recipe, and openly released training corpora (FineMed). It addresses a genuine gap: most open clinical encoders are English, and DoctoBERT is purpose-built for French biomedical/clinical NLP, reporting state-of-the-art results on the public DrBenchmark. The accompanying paper substantiates a clear methodological contribution (medical-term-density filtering plus LLM rephrasing). Marked Assess rather than Adopt because it is a recent beta release from an industry lab (Doctolib) with no independent adoption track record yet, the headline benchmark gains are partly self-reported including a proprietary clinical NER set, and as an encoder it requires downstream fine-tuning to deliver task value. A strong starting point for teams building French clinical NLP; revisit for Adopt once external adoption and reproduction accrue. Training data cataloged separately as finemed (datasets); curation code as doctobert-finemed (software).",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-24",
